hey what is up guys I'm Kay PhD here and  this is the HTC one it's a pretty  awesome phone if you guys haven't  already seen the reviews I'll include my  link to my review as the first link  below the like button on this video but  on the back of this phone there's a  pretty interesting badge  it says Beats Audio it's actually become  one of the selling points of this phone  it's actually one of the most important  things about this phone at least the  speakers themselves are so without any  further ado this is Beats Audio  explained so to be honest Beats Audio  itself isn't actually the most  technically difficult thing to explain  in the world or the most difficult thing  to understand but there is so much  misinformation already out there about  Beats Audio particularly because of word  of mouth and Best Buy stores which I'll  be talking about in a second that it  kind of needs to be explained now a lot  of people already know about beats by  dre headphones those are a pretty much  separate entity but Beats has partnered  with HTC and HP to create devices like  HP laptops and HTC phones that have  Beats Audio built into them what exactly  does that mean well besides all the  marketing BS about how it's supposed to  be the exact representation of what the  artist wants you to hear in terms of  sound quality this is the most technical  video that we could find that you can  find anywhere on the internet of what  exactly Beats Audio is in a smartphone  or a laptop  let's review HD re-engineered the  headphone jack with no metal parts to  reduce ground noise the discreet  headphone amp improves stereo separation  and is more powerful than mp3 players  and other notebook computers the  dedicated audio island isolates the  audio components on the circuit board  minimizing digital interference pressing  function beyond an HP notebook with  Beats Audio will deliver music to your  ears via the headphones or speakers  exclusive to HP notebooks these machines  have been redesigned from the outside in  to deliver the ultimate notebook audio  experience with Beats Audio so the first  ones on our list are overall nice  touches they're actually pretty decent  things to have when you're talking about  audio especially a dedicated amp to  drive higher powered headphone  and for better stereo separation etc  that's pretty decent but it's really all  about that last point when you consider  Beats Audio and difference it makes  versus other devices that don't have  Beats Audio it's all about the Beats  Audio profile which is basically an  equalizer to understand Beats Audio you  have to understand what an equalizer is  so an equalizer basically human hearing  can already hear between about 20 Hertz  and 20,000 Hertz those are the  frequencies of vibrations that we can  pick up with our ears 20 Hertz being the  lowest of the low basses and 20,000  Hertz being the highest of the highs and  equalizer when you apply it to any sort  of form of audio can sort of enhance  certain portions of that audio to make  it stand out more from the others so if  I boost the audio at 15,000 Hertz you're  going to hear that portions stand out a  lot more than the other notes that  aren't in that frequency so devices with  Beats Audio built-in actually have two  audio profiles or two equalizers built  in one with Beats Audio on and one with  Beats Audio off the one with Beats Audio  on has a very exaggerated tones on  basically the low and the high end it  exaggerated s' the more interesting base  and high sections and kind of ignores  the Blessed interesting mids and the  beats audio off profile is actually a  bit of the opposite it's not completely  flat it's actually sort of under  exaggerating those interesting profiles  so it's under exaggerating the base and  under exaggerating the highs and leaving  the not so interesting mids to stand out  so when you turn Beats Audio on you  exaggerate the bass and the highs and we  turn Beats Audio off you under  exaggerate the bass in the highs which  creates a pretty big difference between  on and off so when you flick that Beats  Audio on switch on your device that  happen to have Beats Audio built in you  hear a pretty big difference and sound  and this is often what tricks people  into believing that things with Beats  Audio built in are significantly better  than what doesn't have Beats Audio  imagine this imagine you're at a Best  Buy and there are two laptops sitting  next to each other one silver one  without Beats Audio and one black one  with Beats Audio built in and comes with  a pair of beats by dre headphones and  costs five hundred dollars  the person who wants to say the laptop  is going to bring you to the one with  Beats Audio and is going to tell you hey  listen to this track with Beats Audio  turned off we're going to listen to it  it's going to sound a little bit dull  because of that weekend profile and then  he's going to turn Beats Audio on and  you're going to get that strengthened  profile and you're going to be blown  away because that laptop would Beats  Audio turned on sounds great you didn't  even have to touch the laptop in the  silver section you're already convinced  it's going to sound bad because it  doesn't have Beats Audio that's how they  get you that's how they sell you on  buying a laptop that does have Beats  Audio built in you didn't even have to  listen to the one that sounds just fine  over there because you're convinced it  sounds weak like the weak section  profile in the Beats Audio laptop so  yeah when it comes down to it Beats  Audio is less about the physical  differences inside of the phone less  about that amplifier and more about that  equalizer and most people don't realize  it but there are a lot of equalizers in  between the studio making a sound and  your actual ears your headphones for  example have their own equalizer very  few pairs of headphones are perfectly  flat and accurate most of them are going  to exaggerate some sounds here or there  and that's where you get another form of  an equalizer these by dre headphones  themselves have it slightly uneven  frequency response if you look at the  frequency response chart for a pair of  beats by dre headphones you'll see that  they respond much more powerfully to  lower basses and higher highs and they  don't really emphasize the mids as much  so we combine you know very very bass  heavy headphones with very very bass  heavy amplifier you're going to get a  really bass heavy sound and that's  what's going to impress people and make  them think that things with Beats Audio  sound great  I actually was listening to my 80 hm 50s  with the Beats Audio turned off on the  HTC One and it sounded pretty good but  again that's what the headphone jack  built-in I think the speakers on the  front sound phenomenal when you have  Beats Audio turned on or off it's just  about the clarity and the volume that  you get that changes but it definitely  depends on the device you're looking at  definitely be wary of people trying to  sell you stuff because it has Beats  Audio just have a listen to other stuff  around you first and decide it makes  enough of a difference for you so the  overall message of this video is don't  get tricked into buying something just  because it has Beats Audio built in  everyone's got an EQ figure out  yours either way that's been it thanks  for watching this video I'll leave a  video response right below of one of my  previous videos where I compare a pair  of beats by dre headphones that cost  hundreds of dollars more than a pair of  Audio Technica headphones and the  results may be really impressive to you  so that'll be linked both like button or  as a video response or whatever I happen  to do below but either way like I said  thank you for watching and I'll talk to  you guys in the next video peace  you
 

